  IconPath: icons/magic/symbols/question-stone-yellow.webp
  Description: 'As a bard, you select one muse at 1st level. This muse leads you
    to great things and might be someone you know, a supernatural creature, location,
    deity, philosophy, or captivating mystery. Depending on the type of inspiration
    you receive, your 1st-level muse grants you a specific 1st-level bard feat and
    adds a spell to your repertoire. In addition to this, each muse opens the door
    to many later bard feats. If one type of inspiration is not enough to represent
    your muse, consider the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.Multifarious Muse]
    feat. @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.Enigma] @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.Maestro]
    @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.Polymath] @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.Warrior]'
